@@@!atrep-exo
@=at-usfm=>latex

@@/ Red-letter edition: the words of Jesus in red. Only the
@@/ document rule differs (the class option does the work);
@@/ every other rule and the atrep-bible class asset inherit
@@/ from the base latex surface.

@-> *document
\documentclass[redletter]{atrep-bible}
\begin{document}
\atmaketitle
@(grammata)
\end{document}
>-@
